   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Squiggle\n\nA wavy, zigzag, looping or coiled line draws itself with a springy swim, settles, holds and erases.\n\nCategory: shapes. Length: 2.7 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A title or number needs a lively hand-drawn style underline or flourish.\n- A playful accent line should draw in, wiggle and clear out.\n\nAvoid when:\n- A clean, static divider is needed.\n- The line must connect two specific elements: it is placed at a fixed center and angle.\n\nVariables:\n- shape (enum): Shape, default \"wave\"\n- color (color): Line color, default \"#ffffff\"\n- weight (number, 1-12): Weight, default 3\n- amplitude (number, 0-60): Amplitude, default 14\n- wavelength (number, 12-160): Wavelength, default 48\n- length (number, 40-1200): Length, default 320\n- angle (number, -180-180): Angle, default 0\n- x (number, 0-1): X, default 0.375\n- y (number, 0-1): Y, default 0.5\n- settle (number, 0-1): Settle, default 0.5\n- hold (number, 0-90): Hold, default 12\n- erase (boolean): Erase, default true\n- delay (number, 0-60): Delay, default 0\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
